window.docContents[192].resolve({"/Algebraic-Graph-Theory/#section-the-unlabelled-count":{"contents":"Taking n = k, the cube Q[k] has 2 ^ k * k! automorphisms (as we already knew\nfrom card_aut_hypercube), and dividing the labelled count by this number gives the\nunlabelled count.\n\n/-- The number of subgraphs of Q[n] isomorphic to Q[k]: choose the k free\ncoordinates, then fix the remaining n - k coordinates arbitrarily. -/\ntheorem copyCount_hypercube (n k : ℕ) (h : k ≤ n) :\n    Q[n].copyCount Q[k] = n.choose k * 2 ^ (n - k) := by\n  have hcopy : Q[k].labelledCopyCount Q[k] = 2 ^ k * k.factorial := by\n    rw [labelledCopyCount_hypercube, Nat.descFactorial_self]\n  have hlabel := labelledCopyCount_hypercube n k\n  rw [labelledCopyCount_eq_copyCount_mul_labelledCopyCount,\n    Nat.descFactorial_eq_factorial_mul_choose, hcopy] at hlabel\n  have h2 : 2 ^ n = 2 ^ k * 2 ^ (n - k) := by\n    rw [← pow_add, Nat.add_sub_cancel' h]\n  rw [h2] at hlabel\n  refine Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_right (by positivity : 0 < 2 ^ k * k.factorial) ?_\n  rw [hlabel]\n  ring\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Algebraic Graph Theory\u0009Counting Copies of Subcubes*","header":"12.8.5. The Unlabelled Count","id":"/Algebraic-Graph-Theory/#section-the-unlabelled-count"},"/Connectivity/#section-maximum-degree-two":{"contents":"The results of Cycles In Graphs Of Maximum Degree Two settle the\ncase Δ = 2: a graph of maximum degree at most 2 is 2-colourable unless one of\nits connected components is an odd cycle. Indeed, if it is not 2-colourable then it\nhas an odd cycle, and by Walk.IsCycle.mem_support_of_degree_le_two that cycle\npasses through every vertex of its component. (Since every vertex has degree at most\n2, the component then has no edges other than those of the cycle, so it is an odd\ncycle.)\n\nWe could reduce the problem to connected graphs, since a graph is n-colourable iff\neach of its components is (colorable_iff_forall_connectedComponent, which glues\ntogether colourings of the components using homOfConnectedComponents). But\nWalk.IsCycle.mem_support_of_degree_le_two already works one component at a time, so\nno reduction is needed.\n\ntheorem brooks_two [G.LocallyFinite] (hdeg : ∀ v, G.degree v ≤ 2)\n    (hcyc : ¬ ∃ (u : V) (c : G.Walk u u),\n      c.IsCycle ∧ Odd c.length ∧ ∀ v, G.Reachable u v → v ∈ c.support) :\n    G.Colorable 2 := by\n  apply isBipartite_iff_forall_isCycle_even.mpr\n  intro u c hc\n  by_contra hodd\n  exact hcyc ⟨u, c, hc, Nat.not_even_iff_odd.mp hodd,\n    fun v huv => hc.mem_support_of_degree_le_two hdeg huv⟩\n\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Connectivity\u0009Brooks' Theorem*","header":"10.6.1. Maximum Degree Two","id":"/Connectivity/#section-maximum-degree-two"}});